  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:radio_telescope",
      "title": "Radio Telescope",
      "text": "A dish that listens to the sky: to cold hydrogen, to pulsars. It works by day and in rain, but every machine running nearby is noise in its receiver.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 2$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(thing)Made on the Extreme Assembly Table$() (it is also a crafting table). The recipe pages at the end of this entry - and JEI - show the pattern."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Works day and night, rain or shine, but needs a view of the sky - and every other machine running within 24 blocks raises the system temperature. Tune to the line, narrow the band to it, and integrate long enough: SNR = T\u00b7\u221a(B\u03c4)/T_sys. For pulsars, too wide a band smears the pulse. Every map and record gives Insight."
    },
